.TH "NOTMUCH-INSERT" "1" "Apr 17, 2026" "0.40" "notmuch"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
notmuch-insert \- add a message to the maildir and notmuch database
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.sp
\fBnotmuch\fP \fBinsert\fP [option ...] [+<\fItag\fP>|\-<\fItag\fP> ...]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
\fBnotmuch insert\fP reads a message from standard input and delivers it
into the maildir directory given by configuration option
database.mail_root \%<#\:nmconfig-database\:.mail_root>, then incorporates the message into the notmuch
database. It is an alternative to using a separate tool to deliver the
message then running notmuch\-new \%<#\:notmuch-new-1> afterwards.
.sp
The new message will be tagged with the tags specified by the
new.tags \%<#\:nmconfig-new\:.tags> configuration option, then by operations specified on the
command\-line: tags prefixed by \(aq+\(aq are added while those prefixed by \(aq\-\(aq
are removed.
.sp
If the new message is a duplicate of an existing message in the database
(it has same Message\-ID), it will be added to the maildir folder and
notmuch database, but the tags will not be changed.
.sp
The \fBinsert\fP command supports hooks. See notmuch\-hooks \%<#\:notmuch-hooks-5> for
more details on hooks.
.sp
Option arguments must appear before any tag operation arguments.
Supported options for \fBinsert\fP include
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-folder=<folder>
Deliver the message to the specified folder, relative to the
top\-level directory given by the value of database.mail_root \%<#\:nmconfig-database\:.mail_root>\&. The
default is the empty string, which means delivering to the
top\-level directory.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-create\-folder
Try to create the folder named by the \fB\-\-folder\fP option, if it
does not exist. Otherwise the folder must already exist for mail
delivery to succeed.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-keep
Keep the message file if indexing fails, and keep the message
indexed if applying tags or maildir flag synchronization
fails. Ignore these errors and return exit status 0 to indicate
successful mail delivery.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-no\-hooks
Prevent hooks from being run.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-world\-readable
When writing mail to the mailbox, allow it to be read by users
other than the current user.  Note that this does not override
umask.  By default, delivered mail is only readable by the current
user.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-decrypt=(true|nostash|auto|false)
If \fBtrue\fP and the message is encrypted, try to decrypt the
message while indexing, stashing any session keys discovered.  If
\fBauto\fP, and notmuch already knows about a session key for the
message, it will try decrypting using that session key but will
not try to access the user\(aqs secret keys.  If decryption is
successful, index the cleartext itself.  Either way, the message
is always stored to disk in its original form (ciphertext).
.sp
\fBnostash\fP is the same as \fBtrue\fP except that it will not stash
newly\-discovered session keys in the database.
.sp
Be aware that the index is likely sufficient (and a stashed
session key is certainly sufficient) to reconstruct the cleartext
of the message itself, so please ensure that the notmuch message
index is adequately protected. DO NOT USE \fB\-\-decrypt=true\fP or
\fB\-\-decrypt=nostash\fP without considering the security of your
index.
.sp
See also index.decrypt \%<#\:nmconfig-index\:.decrypt> in notmuch\-config \%<#\:notmuch-config-1>\&.
.UNINDENT
.SH "پیکربندی (CONFIGURATION)"
.sp
Indexing is influenced by the configuration options
index.decrypt \%<#\:nmconfig-index\:.decrypt> and index.header.<prefix> \%<#\:nmconfig-index\:.header\:.-prefix>\&.  Tagging
is controlled by options new.tags \%<#\:nmconfig-new\:.tags> and
maildir.synchronize_flags \%<#\:nmconfig-maildir\:.synchronize_flags>\&.  See
notmuch\-config \%<#\:notmuch-config-1> for details.
.SH "وضعیت خروج (EXIT STATUS)"
.sp
This command returns exit status 0 on successful mail delivery,
non\-zero otherwise. The default is to indicate failed mail delivery on
any errors, including message file delivery to the filesystem, message
indexing to Notmuch database, changing tags, and synchronizing tags to
maildir flags. The \fB\-\-keep\fP option may be used to settle for
successful message file delivery.
.sp
This command supports the following special exit status code for
errors most likely to be temporary in nature, e.g. failure to get a
database write lock.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fB75 (EX_TEMPFAIL)\fP
A temporary failure occurred; the user is invited to retry.
.UNINDENT
.sp
The exit status of the \fBpost\-insert\fP hook does not affect the exit
status of the \fBinsert\fP command.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.sp
notmuch \%<#\:notmuch-1>,
notmuch\-config \%<#\:notmuch-config-1>,
notmuch\-count \%<#\:notmuch-count-1>,
notmuch\-dump \%<#\:notmuch-dump-1>,
notmuch\-hooks \%<#\:notmuch-hooks-5>,
notmuch\-reply \%<#\:notmuch-reply-1>,
notmuch\-restore \%<#\:notmuch-restore-1>,
notmuch\-search \%<#\:notmuch-search-1>,
notmuch\-search\-terms \%<#\:notmuch-search-terms-7>,
notmuch\-show \%<#\:notmuch-show-1>,
notmuch\-tag \%<#\:notmuch-tag-1>
.SH "نویسنده (AUTHOR)"
Carl Worth and many others
.SH "حق نشر (COPYRIGHT)"
